%N A401269 Primes p such that the Euclidean algorithm quotients for the ratio p/q, where q is the next prime after p, are all prime numbers (excluding the integer part zero and the initial quotient 1).
%C A401269 Let p = prime(n) and q = prime(n+1). This sequence lists the primes p for which every partial quotient in the continued fraction expansion of p/q is a prime number (evaluating the tail of the Euclidean algorithm, ignoring initial nonprime structural constants).
%e A401269 For p = 11, the next prime is q = 13. The continued fraction expansion of 11/13 is [0; 1, 5, 2]. Excluding the initial 0 and 1, the remaining partial quotients are 5 and 2. Since both 5 and 2 are prime, 11 is in the sequence.
%e A401269 For p = 347, the next prime is q = 349. The continued fraction expansion of 347/349 is [0; 1, 173, 2]. Excluding the initial 0 and 1, the remaining partial quotients are 173 and 2. Since both are prime, 347 is in the sequence.
%o A401269 (PARI) isok(p) = { if(isprime(p), my(q = nextprime(p+1)); my(cf = contfrac(p/q)); for(i=3, #cf, if(!isprime(cf[i]), return(0)); ); 1, 0) }
%Y A401269 Cf. A000040.
